    "gold_solution": "```python\nimport math\nfrom gurobipy import *\n\ndef solve_problem():\n    m = Model(\"VRPTW\")\n    m.setParam('TimeLimit', 300)\n\n    # --- Data ---\n    n_customers = 5\n    n_vehicles = 4\n    Q = 46  # vehicle capacity\n    vehicle_fixed_cost = 100.0\n    depot = [50, 50]\n    customers = [[26, 79], [33, 64], [27, 45], [20, 67], [15, 86]]\n    demands = [6, 8, 15, 23, 10]\n    time_windows = [[0, 307], [55, 120], [21, 96], [19, 81], [38, 109], [67, 144]]\n    service_times = [6, 13, 6, 7, 5]\n\n    # Node 0 = depot, nodes 1..N = customers\n    N = n_customers\n    nodes = list(range(N + 1))\n    cust_nodes = list(range(1, N + 1))\n\n    # Coordinates: index 0 = depot, 1..N = customers\n    coords = [depot] + customers\n\n    # COMPUTE distance matrix from coordinates\n    dist = {}\n    for i in nodes:\n        for j in nodes:\n            if i != j:\n                dist[(i,j)] = math.sqrt(\n                    (coords[i][0]-coords[j][0])**2 +\n                    (coords[i][1]-coords[j][1])**2)\n\n    # Service time by node (depot = 0)\n    svc = [0] + service_times\n\n    # Big-M for time linking\n    T_max = time_windows[0][1]\n    max_svc = max(service_times)\n    max_dist = max(dist.values())\n    M = T_max + max_svc + max_dist + 1\n\n    # --- Variables ---\n    # Arc variables (binary)\n    x = {}\n    for i in nodes:\n        for j in nodes:\n            if i != j:\n                x[(i,j)] = m.addVar(vtype=GRB.BINARY, name=f\"Arc_{i}_{j}\")\n\n    # Load variables (MTZ subtour elimination)\n    u = {}\n    for i in cust_nodes:\n        u[i] = m.addVar(lb=demands[i-1], ub=Q, vtype=GRB.CONTINUOUS, name=f\"Load_{i}\")\n\n    # Time variables\n    t = {}\n    for i in nodes:\n        a, b = time_windows[i]\n        t[i] = m.addVar(lb=a, ub=b, vtype=GRB.CONTINUOUS, name=f\"Time_{i}\")\n    # Fix depot departure to time 0\n    t[0].ub = 0.0\n\n    # --- Objective ---\n    # Minimize travel distance + vehicle fixed costs\n    obj = quicksum(dist[(i,j)] * x[(i,j)] for i in nodes for j in nodes if i != j)\n    obj += quicksum(vehicle_fixed_cost * x[(0,j)] for j in cust_nodes)\n    m.setObjective(obj, GRB.MINIMIZE)\n\n    # --- Constraints ---\n    # 1. Each customer has exactly one outgoing arc\n    for i in cust_nodes:\n        m.addConstr(\n            quicksum(x[(i,j)] for j in nodes if j != i) == 1,\n            name=f\"VisitOut_C{i}\")\n\n    # 2. Each customer has exactly one incoming arc\n    for j in cust_nodes:\n        m.addConstr(\n            quicksum(x[(i,j)] for i in nodes if i != j) == 1,\n            name=f\"VisitIn_C{j}\")\n\n    # 3. At most K vehicles leave the depot\n    m.addConstr(\n        quicksum(x[(0,j)] for j in cust_nodes) <= n_vehicles,\n        name=\"VehicleLimit\")\n\n    # 4. MTZ subtour elimination\n    for i in cust_nodes:\n        for j in cust_nodes:\n            if i != j:\n                m.addConstr(\n                    u[i] - u[j] + Q * x[(i,j)] <= Q - demands[j-1],\n                    name=f\"MTZ_{i}_{j}\")\n\n    # 5. Time linking: if arc (i,j) is used, arrival at j >= departure from i\n    for j in cust_nodes:\n        for i in nodes:\n            if i != j:\n                m.addConstr(\n                    t[i] - t[j] + M * x[(i,j)] <= M - svc[i] - dist[(i,j)],\n                    name=f\"TimeLink_{i}_{j}\")\n\n    m.optimize()\n    return m\n```",
    "LLM_description": "To: Distribution Planning and Fleet Operations\nFrom: Logistics Operations Manager\nSubject: Routing and Scheduling Plan for Today\u2019s Deliveries\n\nContext\nWe will execute today\u2019s deliveries using a fleet of identical vehicles operating from a single central depot. All vehicles must leave the depot at time 0, complete their assigned stops, and return before the depot\u2019s closing time specified in the data annex. The day\u2019s work involves serving all customers listed in the annex, each located at a defined coordinate on our service map and each with its own delivery requirements.\n\nChallenge Overview\nThe key challenge is to assign customers to vehicles and sequence the visits so that each customer is visited exactly once, service begins within the customer\u2019s allowable time window, and every vehicle returns to the depot before the end of the planning horizon. Each vehicle will make exactly one trip today: depart at time 0, visit a sequence of customers, and return to the depot.\n\nOperating Rules and Constraints\n- Time windows and waiting:\n  - Each customer has an earliest and latest acceptable service start time. Service must start within this window.\n  - If a vehicle arrives early, it must wait until the window opens; it may not start service before the earliest time.\n- Service times:\n  - Each stop requires a defined unloading/service duration. A vehicle departs the customer once service is complete.\n- Capacity:\n  - Vehicles are identical and have the same carrying capacity. The total demand assigned to any vehicle route must not exceed this capacity at any point in the route.\n  - No split deliveries; each customer\u2019s full demand is delivered by a single vehicle on a single visit.\n- Trip structure and return:\n  - Each vehicle departs at time 0 and must return to the depot before the closing time indicated in the annex. No mid-route reloading or multiple tours.\n- Travel times and distances:\n  - Travel time between any two locations is equal to the straight-line distance between their coordinates. We assume an implicit speed of 1, so a distance of X corresponds to X units of travel time.\n\nCost Considerations\n- Deploying a vehicle incurs a fixed cost in addition to distance-based travel cost. The plan should avoid unnecessary vehicle deployments while ensuring on-time service and capacity compliance.\n- There is a trade-off between adding vehicles (which can shorten travel sequences and reduce late arrivals) and the fixed cost incurred by each deployed vehicle.\n\nGoal\nIdentify a set of routes\u2014one per deployed vehicle\u2014that:\n- Visit every customer exactly once,\n- Start service within each customer\u2019s time window (waiting if early),\n- Respect vehicle capacity limits throughout the route,\n- Begin at time 0 and return to the depot before closing time,\n- Minimize the sum of total travel distance and vehicle deployment costs.\n\nNext Steps\n- Confirm all customer time windows, service times, and demands as per the annex.\n- Generate feasible route options that respect the timing and capacity rules.\n- Select the route set that delivers all customers within their windows at the lowest combined travel and deployment cost.\n\nANNEX \u2013 Operations Data\n- Depot location (coordinates): (50, 50)\n- Depot latest return time (closing time): 307\n- Customer locations (coordinates): Customer Locations (coordinates):\n  - C1: (26, 79)\n  - C2: (33, 64)\n  - C3: (27, 45)\n  - C4: (20, 67)\n  - C5: (15, 86)\n- Customer delivery demands (units): Customer Demands:\n  - C1: 6 units\n  - C2: 8 units\n  - C3: 15 units\n  - C4: 23 units\n  - C5: 10 units\n- Customer time windows (earliest, latest): Customer Time Windows [earliest, latest]:\n  - C1: [55, 120]\n  - C2: [21, 96]\n  - C3: [19, 81]\n  - C4: [38, 109]\n  - C5: [67, 144]\n- Customer service/unloading times: Service Times (minutes at customer):\n  - C1: 6\n  - C2: 13\n  - C3: 6\n  - C4: 7\n  - C5: 5\n- Vehicle capacity (units): 46\n- Number of available vehicles: 4\n- Fixed deployment cost per vehicle: 100.0",
    "LLM_description_template": "To: Distribution Planning and Fleet Operations\nFrom: Logistics Operations Manager\nSubject: Routing and Scheduling Plan for Today\u2019s Deliveries\n\nContext\nWe will execute today\u2019s deliveries using a fleet of identical vehicles operating from a single central depot. All vehicles must leave the depot at time 0, complete their assigned stops, and return before the depot\u2019s closing time specified in the data annex. The day\u2019s work involves serving all customers listed in the annex, each located at a defined coordinate on our service map and each with its own delivery requirements.\n\nChallenge Overview\nThe key challenge is to assign customers to vehicles and sequence the visits so that each customer is visited exactly once, service begins within the customer\u2019s allowable time window, and every vehicle returns to the depot before the end of the planning horizon. Each vehicle will make exactly one trip today: depart at time 0, visit a sequence of customers, and return to the depot.\n\nOperating Rules and Constraints\n- Time windows and waiting:\n  - Each customer has an earliest and latest acceptable service start time. Service must start within this window.\n  - If a vehicle arrives early, it must wait until the window opens; it may not start service before the earliest time.\n- Service times:\n  - Each stop requires a defined unloading/service duration. A vehicle departs the customer once service is complete.\n- Capacity:\n  - Vehicles are identical and have the same carrying capacity. The total demand assigned to any vehicle route must not exceed this capacity at any point in the route.\n  - No split deliveries; each customer\u2019s full demand is delivered by a single vehicle on a single visit.\n- Trip structure and return:\n  - Each vehicle departs at time 0 and must return to the depot before the closing time indicated in the annex. No mid-route reloading or multiple tours.\n- Travel times and distances:\n  - Travel time between any two locations is equal to the straight-line distance between their coordinates. We assume an implicit speed of 1, so a distance of X corresponds to X units of travel time.\n\nCost Considerations\n- Deploying a vehicle incurs a fixed cost in addition to distance-based travel cost. The plan should avoid unnecessary vehicle deployments while ensuring on-time service and capacity compliance.\n- There is a trade-off between adding vehicles (which can shorten travel sequences and reduce late arrivals) and the fixed cost incurred by each deployed vehicle.\n\nGoal\nIdentify a set of routes\u2014one per deployed vehicle\u2014that:\n- Visit every customer exactly once,\n- Start service within each customer\u2019s time window (waiting if early),\n- Respect vehicle capacity limits throughout the route,\n- Begin at time 0 and return to the depot before closing time,\n- Minimize the sum of total travel distance and vehicle deployment costs.\n\nNext Steps\n- Confirm all customer time windows, service times, and demands as per the annex.\n- Generate feasible route options that respect the timing and capacity rules.\n- Select the route set that delivers all customers within their windows at the lowest combined travel and deployment cost.\n\nANNEX \u2013 Operations Data\n- Depot location (coordinates): {DEPOT_LOCATION}\n- Depot latest return time (closing time): {DEPOT_CLOSING_TIME}\n- Customer locations (coordinates): {CUSTOMER_LOCATIONS}\n- Customer delivery demands (units): {CUSTOMER_DEMANDS}\n- Customer time windows (earliest, latest): {TIME_WINDOWS}\n- Customer service/unloading times: {SERVICE_TIMES}\n- Vehicle capacity (units): {VEHICLE_CAPACITY}\n- Number of available vehicles: {NUM_VEHICLES}\n- Fixed deployment cost per vehicle: {VEHICLE_FIXED_COST}"
